<title>JAPAN: S.Korean refiner renews Gulf crude contract - source.</title>
<headline>S.Korean refiner renews Gulf crude contract - source.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A leading South Korean refiner has reached an agreement with Oman and the United Arab Emirates to renew its term contract to lift crude oil in 1997, trading sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company will lift 10,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) of Omani crude in 1997, the same as in 1996, the sources said.</p>
<p>They said the company would lift a total of 90,000 bpd of Abu Dhabi crude grades next year, up 10,000 bpd from this year.</p>
<p>The Abu Dhabi crudes due to be lifted are Upper Zakum and Murban, they said.</p>
</text>
